    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "SUPERBLY LOCATED 2-3 BEDROOM MID-TERRACE HOUSE.\r\n\r\nJUST A COUPLE OF MINTUES STROLL TO THE TOWN CENTRE AND TRAIN STATION.\r\n\r\n11 Congress Terrace is located right in the hub of Longford Town, just a five-minute walk from the Train station, on the Dublin-Sligo line. Situated in a prime location just off the Athlone Road, a three-minute walk will take you on to Longford’s town centre. To the rear of the property is a garden, \r\ntogether with storage sheds.\r\n\r\nThe very well-maintained accommodation comprises of a kitchen, living room, and small utility at the back porch, all on the ground floor. There are two double bedrooms and a bathroom on the first floor. \r\n\r\nOne of the outstanding features of this property, is the attic space conversion to an office/3rd bedroom, accessed by an attic stair, with a door leading out to the flat roof area at the rear of the property also.\r\n\r\nViewing is recommended by the sole Auctioneers.\r\n\r\nPlease call us on 043 3350555 to arrange your viewing.\r\n\r\nEIRCODE: N39 V0V1"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Kitchen- 4.15x 4.50m\r\n\r\nLiving area- 4.45m x 4.35m\r\n\r\nBedroom 1- 2.35m x 4.50m\r\n\r\nBedroom 2- 4.50m x 2.30m \r\n\r\nOFFICE/Bedroom 3- 4.15m x 3.75m\r\n\r\nBathroom- 2.55m x 1.65m\r\n\r\nUtility \r\n\r\nStorage Room"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Attic converted to provide office space or a third bedroom\r\n\r\nRear Garden with Storage Sheds\r\n\r\nHigh Speed Cablecom Broadband available \r\n\r\nHighly sought-after location\r\n\r\n300m off the N5 to Castlebar\r\n\r\n3 km from the N4, Dublin-Sligo Route\r\n\r\n5 minutes walk to Train Station and The Cathedral\r\n\r\nJust a 10/15-minute walk to The Mall Sports Amenity, with Pool & Gym\r\n\r\nDouble Glazed PVC Windows & Doors\r\n\r\nIdeally suited to both owner occupiers & investors\r\n\r\nMains Water and Sewerage"
